# NOTE: the second hunk below uses minimal (1-line) context rather than
# the repo's usual 3-line diff -u default. That line (admission.datadoghq.
# com/enabled) sits immediately above the block scripts/patches/tags/
# ust-*.patch uses as ITS hunk's leading context, so a normal 3-line-
# context diff here would read past the closing separator into the UST
# banner text that make tags's patch actually rewrites — order-dependent
# breakage. True zero-context (diff -U0) was tried first but is NOT
# reliably applied by this machine's BSD `patch` when combined with the
# preceding (annotation) hunk in the same invocation — verified empirically
# both ways. 1-line context (the blank '#' line before, the closing
# separator after — both unchanged by either patch) is the minimum that is
# both reliable AND order-independent w.r.t. make tags's patch; verified
# with 'patch --dry-run' in both orderings (tags-then-sso, sso-then-tags).
# Do NOT regenerate this hunk with a default 'diff -u' (3-line context) —
# regenerate only the first (annotation) hunk that way.
--- a/deploy/kubernetes/base/services/notification-service.yaml
+++ b/deploy/kubernetes/base/services/notification-service.yaml
